  "See that sandy water pushing out past the waves? That's a rip current.",
  "It can drag you out faster than most people swim.",
  "From the beach, look for three things.",
  "A spot where the waves don't break.",
  "Murky, sandy water.",
  "Foam drifting out to sea.",
  "Watch the water for ten minutes before you paddle out.",
  "Rips get stronger when the swell's up, so check SurfTribe first.",
  "Caught in one? Stay on your board.",
  "Don't fight it. Paddle parallel to the beach till you're out.",
  "If it still has you, wave an arm and yell.",
  "Save it for the next time you paddle out."
